{"id": "EUVD-2026-97065", "enisaUuid": "4fd70e7d-cf48-3f16-aa87-1e5f88fe814b", "description": "pH7Builder (pH7 Social Dating CMS) before 18.5.0 contains a path traversal vulnerability in the picture module deletePhoto() action that allows authenticated members to delete arbitrary files. Attackers can supply ../ sequences in the POST picture_link parameter to remove other members' photos or configuration and cache files, causing content loss and denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T14:58:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T17:01:23", "baseScore": 7.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/pH7Software/pH7-Social-Dating-CMS/commit/2ffa19ac36d58dbaac37e1c4912be469d67ee75c", "https://github.com/pH7Software/pH7-Social-Dating-CMS/blob/v18.4.1/_protected/app/system/core/classes/PictureCore.php#L23-L38", "https://github.com/pH7Software/pH7-Social-Dating-CMS", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ph7builder-before-18.5.0-path-traversal-arbitrary-file-deletion-via-picture-link"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108902", "GHSA-cmhg-xxg9-x9x9"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.38, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a90bc202-e84e-367a-bf75-1b678cc182fc", "product": {"name": "ph7builder", "vendor": {"name": "ph7software"}}, "product_version": "0 <18.5.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0628f9dc-8b6a-3d1b-a2d8-71d4b0696242", "vendor": {"name": "ph7software"}}], "isExploited": false}